{
  "questions": [
    {
      "area": "Users",
      "question": "Who is the primary user — solo PMs, small startup teams, or enterprise product orgs?",
      "options": [
        {"label": "A", "description": "Small product teams (2–10 people) at startups and scale-ups", "tradeoff": "Sweet spot for collaboration features without enterprise SSO/audit complexity"},
        {"label": "B", "description": "Solo PMs and indie founders", "tradeoff": "Simpler to build but the collaboration angle becomes irrelevant"},
        {"label": "C", "description": "Enterprise product orgs (50+ users)", "tradeoff": "Higher value per seat but requires SSO, RBAC, audit logs, compliance — much larger v1 surface"}
      ],
      "recommendation": "Option A — the braindump emphasizes team collaboration, and small teams give us the realtime/multi-user value prop without enterprise overhead in v1."
    },
    {
      "area": "Core loop",
      "question": "What is a single end-to-end session — paste idea, then what gets generated, in what order?",
      "options": [
        {"label": "A", "description": "Paste braindump → AI generates analysis → epics → architecture in one shot, team edits inline", "tradeoff": "Fast time-to-value, but users can't course-correct mid-generation"},
        {"label": "B", "description": "Paste braindump → AI asks clarifying questions → team answers → AI generates docs in stages", "tradeoff": "Higher quality output, but adds friction and slows the demo"},
        {"label": "C", "description": "Paste braindump → AI generates a single combined doc with all sections", "tradeoff": "Simplest UX but loses the structured artifact value"}
      ],
      "recommendation": "Option A — produces three distinct, navigable artifacts (analysis, epics, architecture) that teams can review in parallel; matches the braindump's framing."
    },
    {
      "area": "Data model",
      "question": "What are the primary entities and how do they relate?",
      "options": [
        {"label": "A", "description": "Workspace → Project → Document (analysis, epics, architecture as typed children); comments and presence attached to documents", "tradeoff": "Clean hierarchy, supports multi-project teams, slightly more schema upfront"},
        {"label": "B", "description": "Project → Document; flat, no workspace concept", "tradeoff": "Simpler, but no natural place to scope membership across projects"}
      ],
      "recommendation": "Option A — workspaces are the standard unit for team SaaS and let us scope billing/membership cleanly later."
    },
    {
      "area": "Auth",
      "question": "What auth model — single-user, team workspaces, or invite-based collaboration?",
      "options": [
        {"label": "A", "description": "Email/password + Google OAuth, workspace-scoped membership with invite links, two roles (admin, member)", "tradeoff": "Standard team-SaaS pattern, covers the collaboration story without RBAC complexity"},
        {"label": "B", "description": "Magic-link only, no roles", "tradeoff": "Lowest friction but no admin controls"},
        {"label": "C", "description": "Full SSO/SAML with custom roles", "tradeoff": "Enterprise-ready but heavy for v1"}
      ],
      "recommendation": "Option A — directly answers the open auth question and matches the small-team target."
    },
    {
      "area": "Realtime",
      "question": "What does 'realtime' mean concretely — live cursors, live document updates, or just notifications?",
      "options": [
        {"label": "A", "description": "Live presence (who's viewing) + streaming AI generation visible to all members + comment notifications", "tradeoff": "Delivers the 'team watches AI work' moment, no full collaborative editing complexity"},
        {"label": "B", "description": "Full Google-Docs-style collaborative editing with CRDTs", "tradeoff": "Best-in-class UX but a major engineering investment"},
        {"label": "C", "description": "Polling-based updates every few seconds", "tradeoff": "Cheapest but feels dated"}
      ],
      "recommendation": "Option A — the wow factor is watching AI generate the spec live with teammates; full CRDT editing is overkill for a v1."
    },
    {
      "area": "Integrations",
      "question": "What external dependencies are needed for v1?",
      "options": [
        {"label": "A", "description": "Anthropic Claude API for generation; export to Markdown and Notion", "tradeoff": "Covers AI quality and the most common downstream destination"},
        {"label": "B", "description": "Claude API only, no exports", "tradeoff": "Simpler but spec docs end up trapped in the tool"},
        {"label": "C", "description": "Multi-provider (OpenAI + Claude) plus Jira/Linear sync", "tradeoff": "Broader fit but doubles the integration surface"}
      ],
      "recommendation": "Option A — Claude for generation quality, Markdown + Notion export so teams can move artifacts into their existing workflow."
    },
    {
      "area": "Scale",
      "question": "What scale should v1 be designed for?",
      "options": [
        {"label": "A", "description": "Up to 1,000 workspaces, ~10 users each, ~100 projects per workspace; generation under 30s p95", "tradeoff": "Comfortable headroom for early adoption without over-engineering"},
        {"label": "B", "description": "Single-tenant, low scale, optimize later", "tradeoff": "Faster to ship but rework looms"}
      ],
      "recommendation": "Option A — concrete targets that inform DB choice and streaming architecture without forcing premature scale work."
    },
    {
      "area": "Out of scope",
      "question": "What is explicitly excluded from v1?",
      "options": [
        {"label": "A", "description": "Exclude SSO/SAML, custom AI fine-tuning, mobile apps, Jira/Linear sync, version history beyond last 10 generations, billing/payments", "tradeoff": "Keeps v1 focused on the core 'paste-to-spec' loop"},
        {"label": "B", "description": "Exclude only billing", "tradeoff": "Scope balloons quickly"}
      ],
      "recommendation": "Option A — protects the v1 timeline and forces a sharp product."
    },
    {
      "area": "Success definition",
      "question": "How do we know v1 shipped successfully?",
      "options": [
        {"label": "A", "description": "50 active workspaces in 60 days; 70% of pasted braindumps result in at least one exported or shared spec; median session has 2+ collaborators present during generation", "tradeoff": "Concrete and measurable, ties to the collaboration thesis"},
        {"label": "B", "description": "Generic 'users like it' / NPS only", "tradeoff": "Hard to act on"}
      ],
      "recommendation": "Option A — measurable outcomes that validate both the AI quality and the collaboration premise."
    }
  ],
  "recommendations": [
    {"area": "Users", "recommendation": "Target small product teams (2–10 people) at startups and scale-ups", "rationale": "Matches the braindump's emphasis on team collaboration without enterprise auth complexity."},
    {"area": "Core loop", "recommendation": "Paste braindump → stream three artifacts (analysis, epics, architecture) in one pass; team can edit, comment, regenerate sections", "rationale": "Delivers structured outputs and a clear demo moment."},
    {"area": "Data model", "recommendation": "Workspace → Project → Document (typed: analysis, epics, architecture), with Comments and Presence attached to documents", "rationale": "Standard team-SaaS hierarchy that scopes membership and billing cleanly."},
    {"area": "Auth", "recommendation": "Email/password + Google OAuth, workspace-scoped membership, invite links, admin/member roles", "rationale": "Resolves the open auth question with the lightest model that supports collaboration."},
    {"area": "Realtime", "recommendation": "Live presence indicators, streamed AI generation visible to all members in the workspace, real-time comment notifications", "rationale": "Captures the collaboration wow-factor without committing to CRDT-based co-editing."},
    {"area": "Integrations", "recommendation": "Anthropic Claude API for generation; Markdown and Notion export", "rationale": "Best-in-class generation quality plus the most common downstream destination."},
    {"area": "Scale", "recommendation": "Design for 1,000 workspaces × ~10 users × ~100 projects; generation p95 under 30s", "rationale": "Concrete targets that inform infra decisions without premature optimization."},
    {"area": "Out of scope", "recommendation": "No SSO/SAML, no mobile apps, no Jira/Linear sync, no fine-tuning, no billing, no full version history beyond last 10 generations", "rationale": "Protects the v1 surface and keeps focus on the core loop."},
    {"area": "Success definition", "recommendation": "50 active workspaces in 60 days; ≥70% of braindumps end in an export or share; median session has 2+ collaborators present during generation", "rationale": "Measures both AI quality and the collaboration thesis."}
  ],
  "rewritten_braindump": "# SpecForge — Collaborative AI Spec Generation\n\n## Core Product\n\nSpecForge is a web app where small product teams paste a rough project idea and, within seconds, get back three structured spec documents — a product analysis, an epics breakdown, and a proposed architecture — generated by Claude. Teammates join the workspace, watch the generation stream in real time, comment, edit inline, and export the result to Markdown or Notion. The wedge is the collaboration moment: instead of one PM writing a spec alone, the whole team watches the AI draft it together and sharpens it on the spot.\n\n## Target User\n\nSmall product teams (2–10 people) at startups and scale-ups. Mixed technical level: PMs, designers, engineers. Workspaces typically have 5–10 members and run 10–100 active projects per quarter.\n\n## Core Loop (single session)\n\n1. A user creates or opens a Project inside their Workspace.\n2. They paste a rough braindump into the editor.\n3. SpecForge streams three documents in sequence: Analysis → Epics → Architecture. Generation is visible live to every workspace member currently viewing the project.\n4. Teammates with the project open see live presence indicators and the streaming output as it arrives.\n5. Any member can comment on a section, edit a document, or regenerate a single section with a refined prompt.\n6. Documents are exported to Markdown or pushed to Notion.\n\n## Data Model\n\n- **Workspace** — billing/membership boundary; has many users via Memberships (role: admin or member).\n- **Project** — belongs to a Workspace; has the original braindump and many Documents.\n- **Document** — typed (analysis | epics | architecture); belongs to a Project; stores current content and the last 10 generation versions.\n- **Comment** — belongs to a Document, anchored to a section/range.\n- **Presence** — ephemeral; tracks which users are currently viewing each project.\n\n## Auth\n\nEmail/password and Google OAuth. Workspace-scoped membership via invite links. Two roles: admin (manage members, delete projects) and member (create projects, generate, edit, comment, export). No SSO/SAML in v1.\n\n## Realtime\n\n- Live presence: see avatars of teammates currently viewing the project.\n- Streamed AI generation: tokens stream to every connected member of the project simultaneously.\n- Real-time comment and edit notifications inside the project view.\n\nNo full CRDT co-editing in v1 — edits use last-write-wins with a soft lock and a 'someone else is editing' indicator.\n\n## Integrations\n\n- **Anthropic Claude API** — sole generation provider for v1.\n- **Notion** — OAuth integration to push exported documents into a Notion workspace.\n- **Markdown** — direct download.\n\n## Scale Targets\n\n- Up to 1,000 workspaces, ~10 users each, ~100 projects per workspace.\n- Generation p95 latency under 30 seconds for the full three-document pass.\n- Realtime fanout supports up to 20 concurrent viewers per project.\n\n## Explicitly Out of Scope (v1)\n\n- SSO / SAML / SCIM\n- Mobile apps (responsive web only)\n- Jira, Linear, GitHub issue sync\n- Custom AI fine-tuning or model selection\n- Multi-provider AI (no OpenAI / Gemini)\n- Full collaborative editing with CRDTs\n- Version history beyond the last 10 generations per document\n- Billing, payments, usage metering (closed beta only)\n\n## Success Definition\n\nv1 is successful if, within 60 days of launch:\n- 50+ active workspaces (≥1 generation in the last 14 days).\n- ≥70% of pasted braindumps produce at least one document that is exported or shared externally.\n- Median generation session has 2+ collaborators present during streaming.\n",
  "suggested_action": "run spec-pipeline"
}
